   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The relation gives \\( f'(0) = -1 \\). Differentiate the relation, using the chain rule on each term that holds \\( f \\): \\( f'' = 3 f^{2} f' + 2 x \\).",
         "mathjson": -1
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Evaluate in order at \\( x = 0 \\), feeding each value into the next: \\( f'(0) = -1 \\), \\( f''(0) = -3 \\).",
         "mathjson": -3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Divide each value by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{-1}{0!} = -1 \\), \\( \\frac{-1}{1!} = -1 \\), \\( \\frac{-3}{2!} = -\\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
